{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 9, :comments ["<b>Before him, those who dwell in barren lands</b> — those who dwell in a land of drought. And the correct interpretation in my eyes: owners of ships, as what is written after it, <i>Tarshish and islands</i>, which is like islands of the sea. And Rabbi Moses said: that they are islands whose dwellers are with the jackal in the desert. And it is not correct. And the word ישיבו means that they shall give this constantly, like <i>and he shall restore to the king of Israel</i>. And some say: at the turn of each year they shall give tribute."], :book :psalms, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 72, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Psalms -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/tehilim"] ["Wikisource Mikraot Gedolot" "http://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Mikraot_Gedolot/"] ["Tanakh, Venice, 1617-1619" "https://dlib.rsl.ru/viewer/01007514045#?page=4"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:34:00.209736144Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}